// The estate: the sample house Sample mode shows ("Preview a finished house",
// through sample_house.js) and the public demo's main house (tools/demo/
// fake_hass.js). A sample layout on three floors: a walk-out lower floor
// (games room, guest suite, media room, workshop), the main floor (living
// room, kitchen, sunroom, primary suite, garage) and an upper floor (a study
// over the foyer, and an office, a loft, a dressing room and a bathroom over
// the garage). Its stairs, as built in Live Aboard: an L-shaped flight with
// two landings from the tall foyer up to the study (raised over it), back
// stairs from the living room up to the office, and a few steps from the
// sunken garage up into the laundry; a straight flight goes down to the lower
// floor. Every name, entity id and label here is made up, and nothing of
// anyone's addresses, devices or people is in it.
// Rooms and positions are plan metres. ?house=classic serves the old house
// (fixture.js) instead, as do ?fresh=1 and the Setup Wizard (website demo).
//
// estateFixture(q) takes the page's query (URLSearchParams) and answers
// {MODEL, STATES, HOUSE3D, WALKERS, MOTION}: the model_get payload, the Home
// Assistant states, the 3D file's furniture and stairs, who walks where (two
// residents with their phones, a guest wearing a visitor tag, and the keys),
// and the motion sensor of each room. ?night=1 shows it after dark: the sun
// down and the lived-in rooms lit. ?sky= sets the weather (as fixture.js).
// The data below is the house; the function after it dresses it for a visit.

